1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:00,810
How long until they

2
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:02,090
reach the rock?

3
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:04,570
Two miles of open sand.

4
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:05,890
Forty minutes,

5
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:06,920
maybe less.

6
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:08,500
No walls.

7
00:00:08,530 --> 00:00:09,850
No guns.

8
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:10,880
No time.

9
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:12,820
But he has diesel.

10
00:00:12,850 --> 00:00:15,210
Eight hundred gallons.

11
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:16,710
He drags the first drum

12
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:18,020
down the rocks.

13
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:19,450
At the edge,

14
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:20,710
the sand narrows.

15
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:22,330
Twelve feet wide.

16
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:24,030
He digs a trench

17
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:26,170
and pours two hundred gallons.

18
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:27,720
The first zombies

19
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:28,800
reach the trench.

20
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:30,410
He lights it.

21
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:32,150
A wall of fire.

22
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:33,980
The first wave stops.

23
00:00:34,510 --> 00:00:35,620
It works.

24
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:36,430
For now.

25
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,340
Then the tide turns,

26
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:40,390
and the sea swallows the sand.

27
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:42,240
The fire dies.

28
00:00:42,270 --> 00:00:43,620
The causeway is gone.

29
00:00:44,150 --> 00:00:45,320
But he just burned

30
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:46,630
a quarter of his fuel.

31
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:48,420
And the smoke is rising,

32
00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:49,420
a thousand feet.

33
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:51,780
Visible from thirty miles.

34
00:00:51,810 --> 00:00:53,660
Someone is going to see it.

35
00:00:54,190 --> 00:00:59,530
Part four. Someone saw the smoke. Follow for part four.
